# Fixture: MQTT JSON payloads shaped like a Theengs-style BLE-to-MQTT bridge (e.g.
# TheengsGateway, github.com/theengs/gateway -- settings.mqtt.gen1TopicPrefix defaults to
# 'home/TheengsGateway') publishing decoded Kegtron Gen 1 (KT-100/KT-200) advertisements.
#
# IMPORTANT PROVENANCE NOTE (see mqttSource.ts's header comment and task-7-report.md
# "Deviations"/"Concerns" for the full citation trail): as of this task's mandatory
# external verification (2026-07-28), Theengs Decoder has NO built-in Kegtron device
# profile -- checked live against https://github.com/theengs/decoder/tree/development/src/devices
# (123 device .h files, none matching kegtron/KT100/KT200) and the compatible-devices doc
# site's page index. There is therefore no real, confirmed wire format to transcribe here
# (unlike udp-packets.jsonl, which was transcribed directly from Kegtron's own UDP
# Streaming PDF spec). This fixture instead models Theengs' GENERAL MQTT envelope
# conventions -- top-level "model_id"/"model"/"brand"/"mac" alongside flat device-specific
# properties, verified against real Theengs device definitions such as
# https://github.com/theengs/decoder/blob/development/src/devices/T201_json.h -- combined
# with the Kegtron-specific property names verified from the real kegtron-ble reference
# decoder (https://github.com/Bluetooth-Devices/kegtron-ble/blob/main/src/kegtron_ble/parser.py),
# whose Home Assistant SensorLibrary keys are volume_start / volume_dispensed / keg_size,
# published there in LITERS (HA's native unit for those sensor classes). This is a
# documented BEST-EFFORT inference, not a confirmed real payload.
#
# Lines starting with '#' are fixture documentation, skipped by the test's loader (same
# convention as udp-packets.jsonl).

# --- KT-200 (dual port), MAC aa:bb:cc:11:22:33 -----------------------------------------
# port 0: initial snapshot (volume_start=5.0L, volume_dispensed=1.000L, keg_size=18.927L
# i.e. a 5-gallon Corny keg per kegtron-ble's KEGTRON_SIZE_DICT[18927]).
{"model_id":"KT-200","model":"KT-200","brand":"Kegtron","mac":"AA:BB:CC:11:22:33","port_index":0,"volume_start":5.0,"volume_dispensed":1.000,"keg_size":18.927}
# port 0: second snapshot -- a full pour lifecycle (below-threshold + settle) is covered
# exhaustively by pourSynth.test.ts; here we just confirm a rise still flows through as a
# second volume_update, without re-firing device_discovered for the same MAC+port.
{"model_id":"KT-200","model":"KT-200","brand":"Kegtron","mac":"AA:BB:CC:11:22:33","port_index":0,"volume_start":5.0,"volume_dispensed":1.355,"keg_size":18.927}
# port 1: a different port on the SAME MAC -- distinct MonitorRef, distinct device_discovered.
{"model_id":"KT-200","model":"KT-200","brand":"Kegtron","mac":"AA:BB:CC:11:22:33","port_index":1,"volume_start":3.0,"volume_dispensed":0.500,"keg_size":18.927}

# --- Non-Kegtron Theengs device sharing the same topic tree -- must be filtered out ----
{"model_id":"T201","model":"TH Sensor","brand":"Oria","mac":"11:22:33:44:55:66","tempc":21.4,"hum":45.0}

